  "lineage": "Ritual singing of the Tuvan kham (shaman), whose algysh, sung invocations and blessings addressed to spirits, are performed in healing and purification rites to the beat of the dungur, a handled frame drum struck with a beater, represented here by the generic frame-drum card. Shamanic practice re-emerged publicly in Kyzyl after the Soviet period through shaman societies such as Dungur, founded under the ethnographer Mongush Kenin-Lopsan.",
